Foveated layers, opaque focus (Quad Views 0024, dcsvr_two_layers_alpha=3): the focus layer comes with no blend flags,
so 0089's rule (the one projection layer that does not blend is the periphery) names no layer and the widest field of
view, which an untracked first frame gets wrong, would decide. With every projection layer of the frame opaque the layer
order decides instead: Quad Views submits each periphery layer first and its focus layer directly after it, so the
first projection layer is the periphery. The flight log's role records (foveated_mode result=3) carry b bit 9 (512)
when the order named the role. New test xrfg_layer_two_layers_deep_hold_roles_opaque: 0089's roles test (unfilled,
wide first focus field of view) with the focus layer opaque and cut to a rectangle (imageRect 2,2 4x4 of 8x8), the
rectangle checked on every frame the fake runtime gets (its focus alpha check is left out: the runtime ignores an opaque layer's alpha). A frame with a blending focus layer is decided as before.

